        "desc": "Conceived and nurtured through voluntary community efforts over three decades, Zinda Park spans over 150 lush acres in Daudpur Union of Rupganj. The self-sustaining green sanctuary boasts thousands of native trees, whispering pine groves, tranquil lotus ponds, and charming wooden footbridges. Visitors can stroll along tree-canopied earthen trails, rent wooden boats for relaxed rowing, and explore an architecturally striking brick library nestled on an islet. Designed with ecological sustainability and community ownership at its heart, the park operates without commercial blare, offering an idyllic respite for families and nature lovers. Cozy dining pavilions serve authentic rural meals prepared using fresh local produce.",
