        "desc": "Constructed in 1986 across the confluence of the Muhuri and Kalidas-Pahalia rivers in Sonagazi, the Muhuri Project is Bangladesh's second-largest irrigation and flood-control barrage. The engineering marvel features a 40-vent automated water regulator that tames seasonal tidal surges from the Bay of Bengal while irrigating over 27,000 hectares of fertile farmland. The reservoir is enveloped by expansive earthen dikes, lush acacia groves, tranquil artificial lakes, and golden reed beds that host thousands of migratory birds during winter. Travelers flock here for exhilarating speed-boat rides, scenic fishing excursions, and breathtaking sunset panoramas over shimmering open waters. Modern guest amenities, breezy picnic grounds, and fish culinary stalls make it Feni's premier tourist destination.",
