        "desc": "The Bishkhali Riverbank offers an awe-inspiring natural escape where one of southern Bangladesh's most powerful tidal rivers flows toward the sea. Stretching along vast embankments, the riverbank provides sweeping, unobstructed views of wide rippling waters, distant green chars, and traditional fishermen casting large circular nets from wooden dinghies. During the late afternoon, the river takes on shimmering golden tones as the sunset reflects across the vast water surface. Visitors enjoy relaxing along the breezy embankments, tasting freshly caught hilsa fish at local riverside eateries, and soaking in the untouched peaceful atmosphere. It is a premier location for photography and peaceful nature appreciation.",
