        "desc": "Flowing directly past Jhalokathi town, the Sugandha Riverfront is the beloved scenic promenade and recreational hub of the district. The municipal riverfront features paved walkways, decorative garden lamp posts, seating benches, and viewing gazebos where residents and tourists gather to enjoy cool river breezes. The river is constantly alive with the vibrant passage of colorful wooden motorboats, trawlers, and grand passenger launches cruising toward Dhaka. At twilight, the glowing lights of rivercraft reflect brilliantly across the water as riverside tea vendors serve steaming cardamom tea and local delicacies. It represents the quintessential soulful urban waterfront of southern Bengal.",
