        "desc": "The Nalchity Riverbank stretches along the peaceful eastern reaches of the Sugandha River, framed by sweeping paddy fields and thick groves of coconut palms. The gentle slope of the grassy riverbank provides an ideal vantage point for watching the daily rhythms of village river life, from women washing brass vessels to fishermen casting delicate gillnets. Open wooden country boats offer affordable, gentle cruises along the river bends where water birds skim past floating hyacinths. The unhurried pace of life and fresh unpolluted air make it a favorite stop for travelers seeking authentic rural tranquility. It captures the gentle, pastoral soul of Jhalokathi's river country.",
