        "desc": "The Mongla Port Riverfront along the wide banks of the Pasur River offers an exhilarating maritime panorama where industrial shipping activity harmonizes with coastal deltaic nature. The riverfront promenade provides sweeping views of massive international container carriers, tugboats, and naval vessels anchored in the deep river channel against backdrop sunsets. Local water taxis and wooden dinghies ferry passengers across the turbulent waters, offering affordable and scenic mini-cruises past port installations and mangrove banks. Waterfront seafood stalls serve freshly prepared mud crab, tiger prawns, and coastal fish dishes caught directly from the surrounding estuaries. It is a vibrant, breezy destination that captures the dynamic marine spirit of southern Bangladesh.",
