        "categoryBn": "সুলতানি আমলের ঐতিহাসিক শাহী মসজিদ",
        "desc": "Constructed in 1581 AD by Masum Khan Kabuli during the pre-Mughal transitional era, Chatmohar Shahi Mosque is a grand triple-domed sanctuary situated in Chatmohar Upazila. Built with seasoned terracotta bricks and sturdy basalt stone pillars, the mosque displays a harmonious blend of Sultanate architectural curves and early Mughal spatial grandeur. The central high dome is flanked by two smaller domes, resting over three pointed arched entrances ornamented with delicate floral terracotta bands. The peaceful courtyard features a deep historic pond and ancient trees that enhance its spiritual serenity. It stands as a prized destination for architectural historians and cultural pilgrims visiting the region.",
