        "desc": "Panihata-Tarani Hills in northern Nalitabari is an untouched ecotourism paradise where rugged green mountain ridges drop steeply into crystal-clear mountain streams right along the international border. Unlike commercialized parks, this location retains untamed wilderness characterized by whispering bamboo forests, wild wildflowers, and dramatic rocky bluffs. Visitors can trek along shallow rocky streams where cool water washes over smooth river pebbles and gaze at the towering blue wall of the Meghalaya plateau rising directly ahead. The serenity, cool mountain breeze, and absence of crowds make it deeply revered among hikers, backpackers, and solitude seekers. It is widely considered the most poetically scenic natural spot in Sherpur.",
