        "desc": "Originating in the Garo Hills and winding gently through the heart of Sherpur district, the Malijhi Riverbank offers a serene countryside escape. Characterized by curving sandbars, gentle water currents, and shade-giving bamboo groves along its embankments, the river serves as a vital irrigation artery for rural farmers. Strolling down the riverbank in the late afternoon allows travelers to watch local wooden dinghies navigate the current and witness villagers tending mustard and paddy fields. The open river horizon provides beautiful vantage points for catching glowing sunsets over rural water reflections. It offers an authentic, relaxing taste of peaceful riverside life in northern Bengal.",
