        "desc": "The Bhogai River and Border Scenery in the Nalitabari frontier is an exhilarating natural attraction where the turbulent mountain river rushes down from the Meghalaya plateau into Bangladesh over white sand and river rocks. Renowned for its crystalline cool waters and rich deposits of mountain sand and pebbles, the river is constantly alive with traditional stone collectors navigating wooden boats against the gentle rapids. Standing on the riverbank, observers enjoy an unobstructed view of the majestic green mountain wall towering right behind the border fence. The rushing sound of water over rocks combined with fresh mountain air creates an invigorating, restorative environment. It is an unforgettable highlight of visiting Sherpur's northern borderlands.",
